IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgl-written`

-- Tests for sgl-written.l4 (ss 184A to 184G). Expected values were decided from the text before the module was run.
-- Period counting: within 7 days after 1 March 2026 ends on 8 March 2026 (P1, P2); 28 days beginning with 1 March 2026 ends on 28 March 2026 (P10); 15 days from 1 March 2026 ends on 16 March 2026.

§ `s 184A(1), (2) and (9): who may pass resolutions by written means`

-- arguments: a public company; its securities are listed
#ASSERT `s 184A(9) the company is an unlisted public company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(9) the company is an unlisted public company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(9) the company is an unlisted public company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: a private company; an unlisted public company; the resolution is one mentioned in s 175A(1)(a); special notice is required
#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company may pass the resolution by written means` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company may pass the resolution by written means` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company may pass the resolution by written means` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company may pass the resolution by written means` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company may pass the resolution by written means` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company may pass the resolution by written means` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(1) the company is a private company or an unlisted public company` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 184A(3) to (5): when a resolution is passed by written means`

-- arguments: the resolution indicates it is a special resolution; voting rights of members who formally agreed; total voting rights; the percentage the constitution requires if greater than 75%
#ASSERT `s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` TRUE 75 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` TRUE 74 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` TRUE 75 100 (JUST 80) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` TRUE 80 100 (JUST 80) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` TRUE 79 100 (JUST 80) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` TRUE 75 100 (JUST 60) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` FALSE 100 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(3) the special resolution is passed by written means` TRUE 0 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: voting rights of members who formally agreed; total voting rights; the percentage the constitution requires if greater than a majority
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` 51 100 NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` 50 100 NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` 60 100 (JUST 60) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` 59 100 (JUST 60) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` 51 100 (JUST 60) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the formal agreements represent the majority the subsection requires` 51 100 (JUST 40) EQUALS TRUE
-- arguments: the resolution indicates it is a special resolution; voting rights who agreed; total voting rights; the percentage the constitution requires
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the ordinary resolution is passed by written means` FALSE 51 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the ordinary resolution is passed by written means` TRUE 51 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the ordinary resolution is passed by written means` FALSE 50 100 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4) the ordinary resolution is passed by written means` FALSE 0 0 NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: the resolution indicates it is one mentioned in s 76(9B)(e); all the members entitled to vote have formally agreed
#ASSERT `s 184A(4A) the resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) is passed by written means` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4A) the resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) is passed by written means` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(4A) the resolution mentioned in section 76(9B)(e) is passed by written means` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: the company receives a document; it is in legible form; it indicates agreement by signature; it includes the text of the resolution; the member had a legible text beforehand
#ASSERT `s 184A(5) the resolution is formally agreed by the member` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(5) the resolution is formally agreed by the member` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(5) the resolution is formally agreed by the member` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(5) the resolution is formally agreed by the member` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(5) the resolution is formally agreed by the member` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(5) the resolution is formally agreed by the member` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(6) subsection (3), (4) or (4A) requires the requisite number of members to formally agree to the resolution on a single day` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: legible before being sent; does not change form; agreed form; can be received legible or made legible
#ASSERT `s 184A(6A) the thing is in legible form or a permitted alternative form` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(6A) the thing is in legible form or a permitted alternative form` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(6A) the thing is in legible form or a permitted alternative form` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(6A) the thing is in legible form or a permitted alternative form` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184A(7) the reference to the passing or making of a resolution includes its passing by written means` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(7) the reference to the passing or making of a resolution includes its passing by written means` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184A(8) the reference to the doing of a thing at a general meeting includes the passing of a resolution authorising it by written means` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184A(8) the reference to the doing of a thing at a general meeting includes the passing of a resolution authorising it by written means` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 184B and 184C`

-- arguments: a private company or an unlisted public company; agreement first sought by the directors under s 184C; a requisition first given under s 183 and the s 183(3A) documents served; the constitution prohibits written means; all constitution conditions are met
#ASSERT `s 184B(1) the resolution may be passed by written means` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184B(1) the resolution may be passed by written means` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184B(1) the resolution may be passed by written means` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184B(1) the resolution may be passed by written means` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184B(1) the resolution may be passed by written means` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184B(1) the resolution may be passed by written means` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: the resolution was passed by written means; the answer under subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 184B(2) the resolution is invalid because it was passed in contravention of subsection (1)` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184B(2) the resolution is invalid because it was passed in contravention of subsection (1)` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184B(2) the resolution is invalid because it was passed in contravention of subsection (1)` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184B(2) the resolution is invalid because it was passed in contravention of subsection (1)` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: the directors wish to seek agreement; the directors have sent each member entitled to vote a copy
#ASSERT `s 184C(1) the directors have sent each member entitled to vote a copy of the text of the resolution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184C(1) the directors have sent each member entitled to vote a copy of the text of the resolution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184C(1) the directors have sent each member entitled to vote a copy of the text of the resolution` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- arguments: complied at the same time; without delay; it was practicable
#ASSERT `s 184C(2) the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184C(2) the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184C(2) the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184C(2) the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184C(2) the directors have complied with subsection (1) as respects every member at the same time and without delay` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184C(3) the directors have complied with subsections (1) and (2)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184C(3) the directors have complied with subsections (1) and (2)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: the resolution is passed before the directors complied; section 184D applies
#ASSERT `s 184C(4) the validity of the resolution is not affected by its being passed before the directors complied with subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184C(4) the validity of the resolution is not affected by its being passed before the directors complied with subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184C(4) the validity of the resolution is not affected by its being passed before the directors complied with subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 184D and 184DA`

-- arguments: a private company or an unlisted public company; voting rights represented; total voting rights; the day the text was sent or the documents served; the day notice was given
#ASSERT `s 184D(1) the member or members may give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` TRUE 5 100 (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184D(1) the member or members may give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` TRUE 5 100 (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 8 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184D(1) the member or members may give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` TRUE 5 100 (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 9 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184D(1) the member or members may give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` TRUE 5 100 (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184D(1) the member or members may give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` TRUE 4 100 (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184D(1) the member or members may give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` FALSE 5 100 (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184D(1) the member or members may give notice requiring a general meeting to be convened for the resolution` TRUE 5 0 (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184D(2)(a) the resolution is invalid because notice was given under subsection (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184D(2)(a) the resolution is invalid because notice was given under subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184D(2)(b) the directors have proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184D(2)(b) the directors have proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184D(2)(b) the directors have proceeded to convene a general meeting for the resolution` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 28 days beginning with 1 March 2026 end on 28 March 2026
#ASSERT `s 184DA(1) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of circulation` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 28 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 184DA(1) the resolution was passed before the end of the period` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 28 3 2026)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184DA(1) the resolution was passed before the end of the period` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 29 3 2026)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184DA(1) the resolution was passed before the end of the period` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
-- arguments: the constitution otherwise provides; the day of circulation; the day the resolution was passed, if it has been; the date asked
#ASSERT `s 184DA(1) the resolution has lapsed` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 28 3 2026)) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184DA(1) the resolution has lapsed` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 28 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184DA(1) the resolution has lapsed` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 29 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184DA(1) the resolution has lapsed` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 29 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184DA(1) the resolution has lapsed` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 29 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: the day of circulation; the day agreement was indicated
#ASSERT `s 184DA(2) the agreement to the resolution is ineffective` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184DA(2) the agreement to the resolution is ineffective` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 29 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 184E to 184G`

-- arguments: the resolution is passed by written means; the earliest day a director or secretary is aware; the day every member had been notified
#ASSERT `s 184E(1) the number of days from the awareness to the last day for notifying members` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `s 184E(1) the company has notified every member that the resolution has been passed in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184E(1) the company has notified every member that the resolution has been passed in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 17 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184E(1) the company has notified every member that the resolution has been passed in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184E(1) the company has notified every member that the resolution has been passed in time` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- time 0 is the day a director or secretary is first aware; the last day, 16 March, is day 15
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 184E(1) the company must notify every member that the resolution has been passed within 15 days` "Gamma Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Gamma Pte Ltd" DOES `s 184E(1) notify every member that the resolution has been passed` AT 15
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 184E(1) the company must notify every member that the resolution has been passed within 15 days` "Gamma Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Gamma Pte Ltd" DOES `s 184E(1) notify every member that the resolution has been passed` AT 16
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 184E(1) the company must notify every member that the resolution has been passed within 15 days` "Gamma Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 16
#ASSERT `s 184E(2) the resolution is invalid because the company did not comply with section 184E` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184E(2) the resolution is invalid because the company did not comply with section 184E` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: the resolution is passed by written means; the company has caused the record to be entered in a book
#ASSERT `s 184F(1) the company has caused the record to be entered in a book` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184F(1) the company has caused the record to be entered in a book` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184F(1) the company has caused the record to be entered in a book` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184F(2) the resolution is invalid because the company did not comply with subsection (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184F(2) the resolution is invalid because the company did not comply with subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184F(3) the record is evidence of the proceedings in passing the resolution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184F(3) the record is evidence of the proceedings in passing the resolution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: a record is made in accordance with the section; the contrary is proved
#ASSERT `s 184F(4) the requirements of this Act with respect to the proceedings are deemed to have been complied with` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184F(4) the requirements of this Act with respect to the proceedings are deemed to have been complied with` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184F(4) the requirements of this Act with respect to the proceedings are deemed to have been complied with` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 184F(5) section 189 applies to the record as it applies to minutes of proceedings of a general meeting` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184F(5) section 189 applies to the record as it applies to minutes of proceedings of a general meeting` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: the company has only one member; the member records the resolution; the member signs the record
#ASSERT `s 184G(1) the company may pass the resolution by the member recording it and signing the record` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184G(1) the company may pass the resolution by the member recording it and signing the record` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184G(1) the company may pass the resolution by the member recording it and signing the record` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184G(1) the company may pass the resolution by the member recording it and signing the record` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- arguments: this Act requires information or a document to be lodged; it is lodged with the resolution
#ASSERT `s 184G(2) the requirement to lodge the information or document is satisfied` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 184G(2) the requirement to lodge the information or document is satisfied` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 184G(2) the requirement to lodge the information or document is satisfied` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulative rules of ss 184C, 184D and 184F: no time limit, no breach path`

-- no time limit and no consequence is stated for these three duties: a late act still reads FULFILLED, and with no act the trace stays RESIDUAL (see NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 184C(1) the directors must send each member a copy of the text of the resolution (no time limit)` "Gamma Pte Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Board of directors` "Gamma Pte Ltd" DOES `s 184C(1) send each member a copy of the text of the resolution` AT 400
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 184C(1) the directors must send each member a copy of the text of the resolution (no time limit)` "Gamma Pte Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 184D(2)(b) the directors must proceed to convene a general meeting for the resolution (no time limit)` "Gamma Pte Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Board of directors` "Gamma Pte Ltd" DOES `s 184D(2)(b) proceed to convene a general meeting for the resolution` AT 400
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 184D(2)(b) the directors must proceed to convene a general meeting for the resolution (no time limit)` "Gamma Pte Ltd" 7 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 184F(1) the company must cause the record of the resolution to be entered in a book (no time limit)` "Gamma Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Gamma Pte Ltd" DOES `s 184F(1) enter the record of the resolution in a book` AT 400
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 184F(1) the company must cause the record of the resolution to be entered in a book (no time limit)` "Gamma Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
